# Figure 56, GBLUR example on the coronagraph's composed detector image (CoroExample.in, element 16, 128 pixels
# of 1.392542e-6): a fresh COMPOSE before each GBLUR, a 0.1 um kernel (far below the pixel: the image is the
# PSF) then a 20 um kernel (14 pixels: the smeared image).  Pages: 0 the INT plot, 1 and 2 the two composites.
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/CoroExample.in fig56
# DEADLINE: 300
cd $TMP/fig56
old CoroExample.in
pgd
/png
mod
ngridpts=128
q
int 16
compose
16
128
1.392542E-06
gblur
1d-7,1d-7
yes
compose
16
128
1.392542E-06
gblur
2d-5,2d-5
yes
dad
! mkdir -p $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/build/figs/fig56; cp $TMP/fig56/giza_*.png $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/build/figs/fig56/
